/* Copyright 2026 Rhett Creighton - Apache License 2.0
 *
 * THE CLASSES OF THING A TRANSLATION UNIT CAN REACH FOR.
 *
 * WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. You cannot decide whether a billion lines of C are
 * malicious. Deciding a non-trivial behavioural property of an arbitrary
 * program is undecidable, so any classifier that tries has misses, and a
 * classifier with misses is not a safety property, it is a hope. This file
 * belongs to a design that asks a decidable question instead: not "is this
 * code bad", but "what can this code reach". The second question the compiler
 * has already answered. Every external entry point a translation unit calls
 * appears as an undefined symbol in its object file, and `nm -u` reads them
 * out. There is no judgement in that step and no model in it either.
 *
 * The measurement that motivated the design, taken on this tree: of 2016
 * objects carrying any undefined symbol, 34 can reach the network, 16 can
 * spawn a process and 4 can load a shared object. Ninety-eight percent of the
 * codebase is incapable of opening a socket. Not reviewed and believed to be
 * incapable. Incapable, because the symbol is not there, and anyone can check
 * that in the time it takes to run nm.
 *
 * WHAT A CLASS IS. A class names a kind of REACH, never a kind of intent.
 * NETWORK is not "code that talks to the internet for a bad reason"; it is
 * "code from which a socket entry point is reachable at link time". A row says
 * what the linker can see, so two people reading it cannot disagree.
 *
 * THE DEFAULT IS THE EMPTY SET. A source file with no row in
 * config/module_capabilities.def declares nothing, and nothing is enforced
 * positively: if it references an entry point in any class here, the build
 * fails. That is the property the whole design rests on. A new file added by
 * anyone, reviewed by no one, cannot acquire the ability to open a socket
 * without a human writing a line that says so.
 *
 * CAP_NONE IS NOT A CLASS AND HAS NO ROW. Its absence is what makes the table
 * closed. An external symbol that appears in no row of
 * config/capability_symbols.def is not "harmless by default" — it is a build
 * failure until somebody classifies it. That is the only arrangement that
 * survives growth: at a billion lines nobody will notice the day a module
 * starts calling a libc entry point that did not exist when the gate was
 * written, so the gate has to notice instead. It costs one row per new libc
 * call across the entire project, because this table is sized by the platform
 * libraries and not by the codebase. The live count is derived by
 * check-capability-closure; a tree a thousand times larger would have a
 * comparable boundary vocabulary.
 *
 * WHAT THIS DOES NOT CATCH, stated here so nobody has to discover it later:
 *
 *   - REACH, NOT LOGIC. A file that legitimately declares CAP_WALLET can still
 *     do the wrong thing with the wallet. Confinement shrinks the surface that
 *     needs human judgement from every file to the few that declared
 *     something; it does not remove the judgement. The point is that the small
 *     set is nameable and the large one never was.
 *   - A HAND-ROLLED SYSCALL. Undefined symbols prove a file does not CALL OUT
 *     to an entry point. A file that issues a raw syscall, or inline assembly,
 *     reaches the kernel with no symbol to see. That hole is closed at source
 *     level by check-capability-closure, not here.
 *   - CODE THAT ARRIVES LATER. A shared object loaded at runtime was never
 *     scanned by anything. CAP_DYNLOAD is therefore the sharpest row in this
 *     file: a hot-swapped worker inherits the capability set of the host that
 *     loaded it and never its own claim, because its own claim is a string
 *     that arrived with the code it describes.
 *
 * Ordering is alphabetical by id and carries no meaning. The gate reads ids,
 * never indices, so a row inserted in the middle changes nothing.
 */

/* ZCL_CAPABILITY_CLASS(id, harm, why)
 *
 *   id    the enum suffix, CAP_<ID>
 *   harm  what an attacker gets if code in this class is hostile, in one line
 *   why   what makes this a boundary worth a declaration rather than noise
 */

ZCL_CAPABILITY_CLASS(NETWORK,
    "sends this machine's data to an address the operator never chose",
    "The only class that can move a secret off the box. Every other class "
    "needs this one to turn a local read into a disclosure, which is why it "
    "is worth declaring even for code that merely dials a known peer.")

ZCL_CAPABILITY_CLASS(PROCESS,
    "runs a program of the attacker's choosing with this process's privileges",
    "A spawn is a total escape: whatever confinement the rest of this table "
    "buys ends at the exec, because the child inherits none of it. Sixteen "
    "objects in this tree can do it and every one of them is a build, boot or "
    "sandbox tool that has to.")

ZCL_CAPABILITY_CLASS(DYNLOAD,
    "executes code that no build, no gate and no reviewer ever saw",
    "The one class whose subject is absent at check time. Everything else "
    "here is a statement about bytes that exist; this is a statement about "
    "bytes that will exist. It is held to a stricter rule for that reason.")

ZCL_CAPABILITY_CLASS(FS_WRITE,
    "alters or destroys files belonging to the operator",
    "Separated from reading because the failures are not comparable. A bad "
    "read leaks; a bad write is not recoverable by re-running anything.")

ZCL_CAPABILITY_CLASS(FS_READ,
    "reads files the operator did not intend this program to open",
    "Broad and mostly benign, and declared anyway: it is the first half of "
    "every exfiltration, and a file that reads nothing is a fact worth being "
    "able to state about most of the tree.")

ZCL_CAPABILITY_CLASS(WALLET,
    "reaches spending material",
    "The one class where a single mistake is unrecoverable and no later gate "
    "can undo it. Named separately from FS_READ even though the key sits in a "
    "file, because 'this code can read a file' and 'this code can read the "
    "key' are not the same sentence and must not compress into one.")

ZCL_CAPABILITY_CLASS(RANDOM,
    "controls values the protocol assumes no one can predict",
    "Not a leak but a weakening, and an invisible one: output from a broken "
    "generator looks exactly like output from a working one. Declared so the "
    "set of files that can influence it stays small enough to audit by eye.")

ZCL_CAPABILITY_CLASS(CLOCK,
    "shifts decisions that are graded against a measured interval",
    "Included because this project already learned it: a wall-clock reading "
    "inside an assertion turns a loaded machine into a red build, which is "
    "why check-no-wallclock-assertion exists. Same reach, same table.")

ZCL_CAPABILITY_CLASS(PRIVILEGE,
    "changes who this process is, or what it is allowed to do",
    "setuid, capset, chroot and the sandbox entry points. Rare, and it should "
    "stay rare: the set of files that can widen their own authority is the "
    "set an auditor reads first.")
